msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

msgid "The set of ground control points a registration was (or will be) solved from. data.points is a list of {id, world:[x,y,z], observations:[{image, pixel:[x,y]}], uncertainty?}; data.crs names the frame the world coordinates are in (null = a site-local grid, which is a different statement from absent). Minimum 3 observed non-collinear points for a similarity to be determined — reported by \\`solvable\\`, enforced by the runner, never at construction (a set being assembled in the field is legitimately incomplete). 1.6.24 (dev30, decided by E.D. 2 Oct 2026, D7): data.control says WHAT the points are — ground\\_control\\_points (default, not written) or camera\\_positions: the GPS positions of the cameras themselves, each point {id, world, image, uncertainty?} with no pixel observation (the camera is where the photograph was taken from, not something seen in it), solvable with three; data.accuracy\\_m is the accuracy the project records for the cameras. A chunk referenced only by its cameras' GPS is placed absolute with such a set, and validate warns «georeferenced only by camera GPS»: absolute without the control said would claim more than the data."
msgstr ""

msgid "*Italiano*: L'insieme dei punti di controllo a terra (GCP) da cui una registrazione è stata (o sarà) calcolata. data.points è una lista di {id, world:[x,y,z], observations:[{image, pixel:[x,y]}], uncertainty?}; data.crs indica il sistema di riferimento delle coordinate world (null = una griglia locale di sito, che è un'affermazione diversa dall'assenza). Servono almeno 3 punti osservati non allineati perché una similitudine sia determinata — lo segnala \\`solvable\\`, lo impone il runner, mai in fase di costruzione (un insieme che si sta raccogliendo sul campo è legittimamente incompleto)."
msgstr ""

